# Build artifacts
build/
# Per-board ESP-IDF build dirs.  main/CMakeLists.txt requires a board flag and
# tells you to keep a separate -B dir per variant (CMake caches the flag), and
# firmware-build.yml uses exactly these names — so building locally the way the
# repo documents produced untracked directories.
build_v*/
*.o
*.elf
*.bin

# Xcode per-user state (snuck into 5f909fc; ignore properly going forward).
**/xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
*.hex
*.map

# Exception: binary test fixtures are source of truth for wire-format tests.
!tests_cpp/fixtures/**/*.bin
# Exception: golden flight log for the flight_report suite (#184).
!tests/test_data/flight_*.bin
# Example flight logs, committed deliberately -- see examples/flights/README.md.
# Only the .bin source and its .json summary; the .csv and _report.html are
# regenerated from the .bin and are several times larger than it.
!examples/flights/flight_*.bin
!examples/flights/flight_*.json
# ...and keep the derived ones out. A flight's CSV is ~4x its .bin and its
# HTML report larger still; both regenerate, so committing them is pure bloat.
examples/flights/*.csv
examples/flights/*_report.html
# The ground-station LoRa log is the exception, because it is not derived from
# anything here: it is a separate capture, written by the receiver on the ground
# rather than by the rocket, and nothing can regenerate it from the .bin. It is
# also what makes the sample flight exercise the report's radio section, which
# the hosted tool would otherwise never show. ~280 KB.
!examples/flights/lora_*.csv

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# macOS
.DS_Store
._*

# KiCad auto-backups. Regenerated by KiCad on every save; ~229 MB across the
# five board projects and pure churn in git. The real history is the commits.
*-backups/

# Finder / iCloud duplicates (files and dirs ending in " 2", " 3", etc.)
* 2.*
* 3.*
* 2/
* 3/

# IDE
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# Generated plots (regenerable from data)
Data_Analysis/plots/
tinkerrocket-sim/plots/
tinkerrocket-sim/*.png
tinkerrocket-sim/*.html
plots/

# Test build artifacts
tests_cpp/build/

# Sim build artifacts — pybind11 outputs land under src/tinkerrocket_sim/
# (depth 3), so a single-segment `tinkerrocket-sim/*.so` would miss them.
tinkerrocket-sim/build/
tinkerrocket-sim/**/*.egg-info/
tinkerrocket-sim/**/*.so

# replay_deployment_detector.py compiles this from the firmware headers on
# demand and rebuilds it whenever they change — committing it would be a stale
# copy of the very thresholds the tool exists to read live.
Data_Analysis/*.so

# Xcode
TinkerRocketApp/DerivedData/
*.xcuserdata

# Claude Code working files
.claude/

# Android release signing — the keystore must NEVER enter the repo
# (docs/android-release-signing.md); belt-and-suspenders for a mis-placed file.
*.keystore
*.jks
